IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei1-rate`

-- Tests of ei1-rate.l4 (Act ss 14, 16 and 17). Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the section
-- named beside the assertion (the table of s 14(2) is transcribed from src:418-427); none is copied from the module's
-- output. One #ASSERT per line.

§ `s 14(2) the weeks by which insurable earnings are divided (src:418-427)`
-- not more than 6%: 22; >6 to 7: 21; >7 to 8: 20; >8 to 9: 19; >9 to 10: 18; >10 to 11: 17; >11 to 12: 16; >12 to 13: 15; more than 13%: 14
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the number of weeks by which the insurable earnings in the calculation period are divided` 0 EQUALS 22
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the number of weeks by which the insurable earnings in the calculation period are divided` 0.06 EQUALS 22
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the number of weeks by which the insurable earnings in the calculation period are divided` 0.0601 EQUALS 21
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the number of weeks by which the insurable earnings in the calculation period are divided` 0.07 EQUALS 21
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the number of weeks by which the insurable earnings in the calculation period are divided` 0.0701 EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the number of weeks by which the insurable earnings in the calculation period are divided` 0.08 EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the number of weeks by which the insurable earnings in the calculation period are divided` 0.0801 EQUALS 19
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the number of weeks by which the insurable earnings in the calculation period are divided` 0.09 EQUALS 19
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the number of weeks by which the insurable earnings in the calculation period are divided` 0.0901 EQUALS 18
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the number of weeks by which the insurable earnings in the calculation period are divided` 0.10 EQUALS 18
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the number of weeks by which the insurable earnings in the calculation period are divided` 0.1001 EQUALS 17
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the number of weeks by which the insurable earnings in the calculation period are divided` 0.11 EQUALS 17
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the number of weeks by which the insurable earnings in the calculation period are divided` 0.1101 EQUALS 16
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the number of weeks by which the insurable earnings in the calculation period are divided` 0.12 EQUALS 16
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the number of weeks by which the insurable earnings in the calculation period are divided` 0.1201 EQUALS 15
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the number of weeks by which the insurable earnings in the calculation period are divided` 0.13 EQUALS 15
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the number of weeks by which the insurable earnings in the calculation period are divided` 0.1301 EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the number of weeks by which the insurable earnings in the calculation period are divided` 0.25 EQUALS 14

§ `s 14(3) insurable earnings in the calculation period (src:429-431)`
#ASSERT `s 14(3) the insurable earnings in the calculation period` 20000 3000 EQUALS 23000
#ASSERT `s 14(3) the insurable earnings in the calculation period` 20000 0 EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT `s 14(3) the insurable earnings in the calculation period` 0 0 EQUALS 0

§ `s 14(4) the calculation period (src:433)`
-- The number of weeks follows the table: 14 at more than 13%, 21 at 6% to 7%.
#ASSERT `s 14(4) the number of weeks in the calculation period` 0.14 EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `s 14(4) the number of weeks in the calculation period` 0.065 EQUALS 21
-- Sixteen weeks of earnings 100, 200, ... 1600 (total 13,600). 14 weeks are the 14 highest: 13,600 less 100 and 200.
`ei1 test sixteen weeks of earnings` MEANS LIST 1600, 100, 1500, 200, 1400, 300, 1300, 400, 1200, 500, 1100, 600, 1000, 700, 900, 800
#ASSERT `s 14(4) the insurable earnings of the weeks in the calculation period` `ei1 test sixteen weeks of earnings` 0.14 EQUALS 13300
-- fewer weeks than the calculation period: all of them count
#ASSERT `s 14(4) the insurable earnings of the weeks in the calculation period` `ei1 test sixteen weeks of earnings` 0.065 EQUALS 13600
#ASSERT `s 14(4) the insurable earnings of the weeks in the calculation period` (LIST 100, 200, 300) 0.14 EQUALS 600
#ASSERT `s 14(4) the insurable earnings of the weeks in the calculation period` EMPTY 0.14 EQUALS 0

§ `s 14(1.1) the maximum weekly insurable earnings (src:412-414)`
-- 1997 to 2000: $750; a later year: the maximum yearly insurable earnings divided by 52 (here 52,000 / 52 = 1,000); before 1997: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 14(1.1) the maximum weekly insurable earnings` (YearMonthDay 1996 12 31) 52000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 14(1.1) the maximum weekly insurable earnings` (YearMonthDay 1997 1 5) 52000 EQUALS JUST 750
#ASSERT `s 14(1.1) the maximum weekly insurable earnings` (YearMonthDay 2000 12 31) 52000 EQUALS JUST 750
#ASSERT `s 14(1.1) the maximum weekly insurable earnings` (YearMonthDay 2001 1 7) 52000 EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `s 14(1.1) the maximum weekly insurable earnings` (YearMonthDay 2026 10 25) 52000 EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `s 14(1.1) the maximum weekly insurable earnings` (YearMonthDay 2026 10 25) 65000 EQUALS JUST 1250

§ `s 14(2) weekly insurable earnings (src:415-416, 412)`
-- args: the insurable earnings in the calculation period, the regional rate, the maximum weekly insurable earnings
-- 22,000 over 22 weeks (rate 5%) is 1,000 a week; 21,000 over 21 weeks (6.5%) is 1,000; 14,000 over 14 weeks (14%) is 1,000.
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the claimant's weekly insurable earnings` 22000 0.05 (JUST 1100) EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the claimant's weekly insurable earnings` 21000 0.065 (JUST 1100) EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the claimant's weekly insurable earnings` 14000 0.14 (JUST 1100) EQUALS JUST 1000
-- never more than the maximum weekly insurable earnings
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the claimant's weekly insurable earnings` 22000 0.05 (JUST 750) EQUALS JUST 750
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the claimant's weekly insurable earnings` 22000 0.05 (JUST 1000) EQUALS JUST 1000
-- no maximum available (a benefit period before 1997): not covered
#ASSERT `s 14(2) the claimant's weekly insurable earnings` 22000 0.05 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 14(1) the rate of weekly benefits (src:410)`
-- args: weekly insurable earnings, paid under section 23 at the 61-week maximum
#ASSERT `s 14(1) the rate of weekly benefits payable to the claimant` 1000 FALSE EQUALS 550
#ASSERT `s 14(1) the rate of weekly benefits payable to the claimant` 1000 TRUE EQUALS 330
-- rounded to the nearest dollar, the higher dollar when equidistant (s 6(2)): 55% of 100.90 is 55.495; of 101 is 55.55; of 50 is 27.5; 33% of 50 is 16.5
#ASSERT `s 14(1) the rate of weekly benefits payable to the claimant` 100.9 FALSE EQUALS 55
#ASSERT `s 14(1) the rate of weekly benefits payable to the claimant` 101 FALSE EQUALS 56
#ASSERT `s 14(1) the rate of weekly benefits payable to the claimant` 50 FALSE EQUALS 28
#ASSERT `s 14(1) the rate of weekly benefits payable to the claimant` 50 TRUE EQUALS 17
#ASSERT `s 14(1) the rate of weekly benefits payable to the claimant` 333 FALSE EQUALS 183
#ASSERT `s 14(1) the rate of weekly benefits payable to the claimant` 0 FALSE EQUALS 0

§ `s 16 the family supplement (src:437, 443)`
-- args: one or more dependent children, establishes the prescribed low-income criteria
#ASSERT `s 16(1) the rate of weekly benefits is increased by the amount of a family supplement` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 16(1) the rate of weekly benefits is increased by the amount of a family supplement` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 16(1) the rate of weekly benefits is increased by the amount of a family supplement` TRUE FALSE)
-- the most the increase may be: the prescribed percentage of weekly insurable earnings, or 25% if none is prescribed (rounded under s 6(2))
#ASSERT `s 16(4) the most that the increase in the rate of weekly benefits may be` NOTHING 400 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `s 16(4) the most that the increase in the rate of weekly benefits may be` (JUST (0.2)) 400 EQUALS 80
#ASSERT `s 16(4) the most that the increase in the rate of weekly benefits may be` NOTHING 333 EQUALS 83
#ASSERT `s 16(4) the most that the increase in the rate of weekly benefits may be` NOTHING 334 EQUALS 84
#ASSERT `s 16(4) the most that the increase in the rate of weekly benefits may be` (JUST (0.1)) 505 EQUALS 51
-- args: the rate increases by a family supplement, the supplement determined under the regulations, the most the increase may be
#ASSERT `s 16(1) and s 16(4) the amount of the increase in the rate of weekly benefits` TRUE 31.3 100 EQUALS 31.3
#ASSERT `s 16(1) and s 16(4) the amount of the increase in the rate of weekly benefits` TRUE 31.3 20 EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `s 16(1) and s 16(4) the amount of the increase in the rate of weekly benefits` FALSE 31.3 100 EQUALS 0

§ `s 17 the maximum rate of weekly benefits (src:445)`
-- 55% of the maximum yearly insurable earnings divided by 52, rounded under s 6(2): 52,000 gives 550; 65,000 gives 687.50, rounded up to 688; 65,700 gives 694.90, rounded to 695.
#ASSERT `s 17 the maximum rate of weekly benefits` 52000 EQUALS 550
#ASSERT `s 17 the maximum rate of weekly benefits` 65000 EQUALS 688
#ASSERT `s 17 the maximum rate of weekly benefits` 65700 EQUALS 695
#ASSERT `s 14(1) and s 17 the rate of weekly benefits, not above the maximum rate` 600 550 EQUALS 550
#ASSERT `s 14(1) and s 17 the rate of weekly benefits, not above the maximum rate` 500 550 EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `s 14(1) and s 17 the rate of weekly benefits, not above the maximum rate` 550 550 EQUALS 550
